title: "Independent Lean 4 Verification of the Complete Smithian Fold Theory Model"
type: article
version: 1.0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21761665
date-released: 2026-08-02
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21761665"
authors:
  - family-names: Smith
    given-names: Maria
    email: Maria.Smith.Sftoe@gmail.com
    affiliation: Ernos Labs
abstract: >-
  Independent Lean 4 verification of the complete registered Smithian Fold
  Theory model as frozen on 2 August 2026. The verification kernel-checks the
  two-class operational root and its unique survivor, checks proof-bearing
  acceptance gates, and traverses the ordered census of 2,777 claims, 898,902
  candidates, 11,108 adverse controls and 17 branches without reported issue.
  The formal scope is stated explicitly: native Lean theorems cover the root
  and generic gate implications, while the remaining scientific statements are
  checked as complete registered artefacts. The result establishes internal
  formal and computational consistency of the frozen corpus; it does not by
  itself establish empirical truth or superiority over every competing model.
keywords:
  - Smithian Fold Theory
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - operational root
  - unique survivor
  - proof-bearing certificates
  - exact arithmetic
  - reproducible science
